$\begin{align*}x^{3}-36x&=0\\x(x-6)(x+6)&=0\\x&=-6,\ 0,\ 6\end{align*}$
For $f(x)=x^{3}-36x$, $f(-x)=-f(x)$, so the two enclosed regions have equal area. On $0<x<6$, $x(x-6)(x+6)<0$, so the curve lies below the $x$-axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.45cm,y=0.025cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{areaFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[areaFill] (-6,0) -- plot[domain=-6:0,samples=80] (\x,{\x*\x*\x-36*\x}) -- cycle;
\fill[areaFill] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:6,samples=80] (\x,{\x*\x*\x-36*\x}) -- cycle;
\draw[->,black] (-7,0)--(7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-95)--(0,95) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,black,<->] plot[domain=-6.6:6.6,samples=120] (\x,{\x*\x*\x-36*\x});
\node[below left] at (-6,0) {$-6$};
\node[above right] at (6,0) {$6$};
\node[below right] at (0,0) {$0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}A&=-2\int_{0}^{6}(x^{3}-36x)\,dx\\&=-2\left[\frac{x^{4}}{4}-18x^{2}\right]_{0}^{6}\\&=-2(324-648)\\&=648\ \text{units}^{2}\end{align*}$
The signed integral over $[-6,6]$ is zero; the total area adds the two positive areas.

For $f(x)=x^{4}-16x^{2}$, $f(-x)=f(x)$, so the graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis.
$\begin{align*}x^{4}-16x^{2}&=0\\x^{2}(x-4)(x+4)&=0\\x&=-4,\ 0,\ 4\end{align*}$
On $0<x<4$, $x^{2}(x-4)(x+4)<0$. The curve stays below the $x$-axis on this half; its contact at $x=0$ does not change the sign.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.04cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{areaFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[areaFill] (-4,0) -- plot[domain=-4:4,samples=120] (\x,{\x*\x*\x*\x-16*\x*\x}) -- cycle;
\draw[->,black] (-5,0)--(5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-75)--(0,35) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,black,<->] plot[domain=-4.2:4.2,samples=140] (\x,{\x*\x*\x*\x-16*\x*\x});
\node[above left] at (-4,0) {$-4$};
\node[above right] at (4,0) {$4$};
\node[above left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}A&=-2\int_{0}^{4}(x^{4}-16x^{2})\,dx\\&=-2\left[\frac{x^{5}}{5}-\frac{16x^{3}}{3}\right]_{0}^{4}\\&=-2\left(\frac{1024}{5}-\frac{1024}{3}\right)\\&=\frac{4096}{15}\ \text{units}^{2}\end{align*}$
